# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore  (what to EXCLUDE from the Docker build context)
# =============================================================================
# The Dockerfiles do `COPY . /app` with the build context set to the repo root
# (see docker-compose). Without this file, that would sweep local-only clutter
# and secrets into every image and slow the build by shipping a bloated context
# to the Docker daemon. Each non-comment line is a path pattern to skip; a
# leading `!` is a re-INCLUDE (an exception to an earlier exclusion).
#
# IMPORTANT: like .gitignore, this format only treats `#` as a comment when it
# is the FIRST character on the line — inline "pattern  # note" is NOT supported
# (the `#` would become part of the pattern). So every note below is its own line.

# The local virtualenv — the image rebuilds it via `uv sync`.
.venv
# Compiled *.pyc caches from any directory depth.
**/__pycache__
# pytest's run cache (dev/CI artifact, not needed at runtime).
.pytest_cache
# ruff's lint cache (dev artifact).
.ruff_cache
# Documentation — not needed inside the runtime image.
docs
# The entire git history (large, and never needed at runtime).
.git
# Local secrets/config: MUST NOT be baked into an image.
.env
# Any environment-specific dotenv variants (also secret).
.env.*
# ...but DO keep the committed, secret-free template file.
!.env.example
